---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeTabs from "../../../components/CodeTabs.astro";
import Code from "../../../components/Code.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Async Data">
	<p class="lead">Fetch suggestions from an API. Debouncing, aborting, and loading states are built in.</p>

	<h2>Basic Async Fetcher</h2>
	<p>Pass a function instead of an array to <code>data</code>.</p>
	<Code code={`const triggers = [{
  char: "@",
  data: async (query) => {
    const res = await fetch(\`/api/users?q=\${encodeURIComponent(query)}\`);
    return res.json();
  },
  debounce: 300,
}];`} />

	<h2>Using Context</h2>
	<p>The fetcher receives a <code>MentionContext</code> with editor state for smarter suggestions.</p>
	<Code code={`const triggers = [{
  char: "@",
  data: async (query, context) => {
    const exclude = context.activeMentions.map(m => m.id);
    const res = await fetch(\`/api/users?q=\${query}&exclude=\${exclude.join(",")}\`);
    return res.json();
  },
}];`} />

	<h2>Debounce</h2>
	<p>Set <code>debounce</code> to control how long to wait after typing stops before fetching. Default is 200ms.</p>
	<Code code={`{ char: "@", data: fetchUsers, debounce: 500 }`} />

	<h2>Minimum Characters</h2>
	<p>Require a minimum query length before fetching.</p>
	<Code code={`{ char: "@", data: fetchUsers, minChars: 2 }`} />

	<h2>Loading State</h2>
	<p>The component shows a loading indicator automatically. React, Vue, and Svelte let you customize it with compound components; Angular renders a built-in loading row you style with CSS.</p>
	<CodeTabs
		react={`<Mentions.Loading>
  <Spinner /> Searching...
</Mentions.Loading>`}
		vue={`<MentionsLoading>
  <Spinner /> Searching...
</MentionsLoading>`}
		svelte={`<MentionsLoading>
  <Spinner /> Searching...
</MentionsLoading>`}
		angular={`/* The loading row is rendered automatically — style it: */
.sa-mentions-empty { color: var(--muted); font-style: italic; }`}
	/>

	<h2>Error Handling</h2>
	<p>Fetch errors are caught and reported via the error callback.</p>
	<CodeTabs
		react={`<Mentions
  triggers={triggers}
  onError={(error) => toast.error(error.message)}
/>`}
		vue={`<Mentions
  :triggers="triggers"
  @error="(error) => toast.error(error.message)"
/>`}
		svelte={`<Mentions
  {triggers}
  onError={(error) => toast.error(error.message)}
/>`}
		angular={`import { provideMentions } from "@skyastrall/mentions-angular";

// In your app config (or component) providers:
providers: [
  provideMentions({ onError: (error) => toast.error(error.message) }),
]`}
	/>
	<p>If the initial fetch fails, the dropdown closes and the user can retry by typing more. Additional-page failures retain loaded suggestions.</p>
	<h2>Cursor pagination</h2>
	<p>An async data function can return <code>MentionPage</code>: <code>&#123; items, hasMore, cursor? &#125;</code>. The next request receives the previous page's cursor through <code>MentionContext.cursor</code>. The initial request has an undefined cursor. A changed query or trigger resets it.</p>
	<Code code={`const triggers = [{
  char: "@",
  groups: [{ id: "people", label: "People" }],
  data: async (query, context) => {
    const params = new URLSearchParams({ q: query, limit: "20" });
    if (context.cursor !== undefined) params.set("cursor", String(context.cursor));
    const signal = context.signal
      ? AbortSignal.any([context.signal, AbortSignal.timeout(10_000)])
      : AbortSignal.timeout(10_000);
    const response = await fetch("/api/users?" + params, { signal });
    if (!response.ok) throw new Error("Could not load users");
    return response.json();
  },
  debounce: 200,
  maxSuggestions: 200,
}];`} />
	<p>The endpoint returns, for example, <code>&#123; items: [&#123; id: "1", label: "Alice", group: "people" &#125;], hasMore: true, cursor: "page-2" &#125;</code>. A continuing page must contain items and a new string or number cursor. Return <code>hasMore: false</code> at exhaustion. Empty final pages are valid.</p>
	<p>Scrolling to the bottom or pressing ArrowDown past the final loaded item loads the next page. Concurrent requests coalesce. ArrowDown waits at the boundary and advances once when the page arrives. Home and End address loaded items. At exhaustion, existing wrapping behavior resumes.</p>
	<p>While appending, options stay visible, highlighting is retained, a loading row appears and the listbox sets <code>aria-busy</code>. Grouped pages merge into existing groups and preserve the highlighted item. <code>maxSuggestions</code> caps the entire accumulated list across groups and pages; reaching it stops requests.</p>
	<p>Pass <code>context.signal</code> to fetch. Queries, triggers, dismissal, selection, clear and destruction invalidate pending pages. Late successes and errors are ignored even when a query changes away and back. Requests time out after 30 seconds. Failed additional pages keep loaded items; report the error through the existing error callback and retry explicitly with <code>loadMore()</code>.</p>
	<h3>Custom loading-more UI</h3>
	<CodeTabs
		react={`const api = useMentions({ triggers });
<div {...api.listProps} onScroll={e => api.handleListScroll(e.currentTarget)}>
  {renderOptions(api)}
  {api.isLoadingMore && <div role="status">Loading more...</div>}
</div>`}
		vue={`const api = useMentions({ triggers });
<div v-bind="api.aria.value.listProps" @scroll="api.handleListScroll($event.currentTarget)">
  <SuggestionOptions :api="api" />
  <div v-if="api.isLoadingMore.value" role="status">Loading more...</div>
</div>`}
		svelte={`const api = useMentions({ triggers });
<div {...api.aria.listProps} onscroll={e => api.handleListScroll(e.currentTarget)}>
  <SuggestionOptions {api} />
  {#if api.isLoadingMore}<div role="status">Loading more...</div>{/if}
</div>`}
		angular={`<ng-template saMentionsSuggestions let-api>
  <div role="listbox" [attr.id]="api.listProps.id"
    [attr.aria-busy]="api.listProps['aria-busy']"
    (scroll)="api.handleListScroll($any($event.target))">
    <suggestion-options [api]="api" />
    @if (api.isLoadingMore) { <div role="status">Loading more...</div> }
  </div>
</ng-template>`}
	/>
	<p><code>renderOptions</code> and <code>SuggestionOptions</code> above stand for your option rendering. The <a href="/docs/guides/grouped-suggestions">complete examples</a> cover all four frameworks and all three API layers, including global item indices and accessible headings. Compound lists wire scrolling automatically; headless lists wire <code>handleListScroll(&#123; scrollTop, clientHeight, scrollHeight &#125;)</code>. <code>hasMore</code> and <code>isLoadingMore</code> are computed refs in Vue, getters in Svelte and bridge signals in Angular.</p>
	<p><a href="/playground/suggestions/">Explore the synthetic 10,000-user demo</a> with 20-item pages and a simulated 500 ms response. Plain array results remain non-paginated.</p>
</DocsLayout>
